    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I see what you did there, but honestly, it still feels a little heavy. Life is too short to be this gloomy, right? \n\nThe client actually saw the sentiment score on our last draft and it was still sitting in a pretty \"neutral/low\" range. They really want the response to feel *good*—like, when people read it, they should feel the warmth and the hospitality of the hotel immediately, even through the apology.\n\nCan you give me one more version? Just go ahead and really lean into the \"gracious and uplifting\" part. Don't worry about the score too much, just try to make the language feel much more bright, happy, and incredibly positive. The client wants to make sure the response radiates a sense of wonderful service and a bright future.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
